            <ArticleTitle>Posttraumatic coronary artery-right ventricular fistula with multiple ventricular septal defects.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>670-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2010.01032.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The combination of posttraumatic coronary artery-right ventricular fistula and multiple ventricular septal defects is a rare and interesting phenomenon. We describe a case of a 19-year-old male with these findings following a blunt chest trauma after a motorcycle accident.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
